From: Mohammed <91819504+mohammed7s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:04:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cp2a: enable Computer Control with per-app consent and
 version 5

Turn on these android.companion.virtualdevice.flags, READ_ONLY like the
other Computer Control flags already enabled in this release config:

 - computer_control_access: without it ACCESS_COMPUTER_CONTROL is not
   defined and VirtualDeviceManagerService refuses every session request.
 - computer_control_per_app_consent: without it the user cannot approve
   or revoke an agent per target app, and the Settings pages that manage
   this are hidden.
 - computer_control_support_v5: the service advertises version 5, whose
   sessions require a foreground window. The frameworks/base changes
   reject version 4 requests so that this check cannot be avoided.

This only makes the feature reachable. No app can use it until the user
allows an agent and its target apps in Settings, and the agent must also
hold the assistant role (computer_control_role_assistant_requirement is
already enabled here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
